{
  "result": "The morning begins quietly in my small kitchen before the rest of the house has fully awakened. Light falls across the wooden table where a mug stands empty and waiting beside a chipped plate. I like this hour because it belongs to no one in particular and asks nothing from me except attention.\n\nI fill the kettle and listen for the soft change in its sound as the water begins to warm. Outside the window a neighbor walks a dog past wet leaves while somewhere a radio plays a familiar song. There is no hurry in these small actions and that is precisely why they matter so much to me.\n\nI place bread in the toaster and watch the coils glow orange before they fade again. Butter melts slowly and pools in the warm crumb while I open a book I have been reading all week. The words are not important right now and the story can wait until later when the day is fully underway. What matters is the steam rising from the mug and the quiet way it curls toward the ceiling.\n\nI think about plans I have made and about worries I have carried for far too long during recent nights. In this warm room both kinds of thoughts feel lighter and somehow easier to set down for a while. When the house finally stirs I will be ready to join the noise with an open and patient heart. For now I simply breathe slowly and smile.",
